WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.766 --> 00:00:14.968
Once upon a time, there was an old shoemaker.

2
00:00:16.429 --> 00:00:18.990
Although he worked hard, he was very poor.

3
00:00:20.111 --> 00:00:23.112
One cold winter night, he sat at his workbench.

4
00:00:24.053 --> 00:00:26.154
He began cutting his last piece of leather.

5
00:00:27.174 --> 00:00:29.616
There was only enough for one pair of shoes.

6
00:00:33.288 --> 00:00:35.970
"Come to bed, dear," his wife said.

7
00:00:37.311 --> 00:00:38.812
The shoemaker shook his head.

8
00:00:38.832 --> 00:00:43.515
"If I don't sell these shoes, we'll have no money."

9
00:00:43.535 --> 00:00:48.178
"You can finish them in the morning," the wife said.

10
00:00:48.198 --> 00:00:51.180
"Please, get some rest."

11
00:00:52.561 --> 00:00:55.443
The shoemaker sighed and put down his scissors.

12
00:00:57.885 --> 00:01:01.768
In the middle of the night, two little elves climbed onto the workbench.

13
00:01:03.388 --> 00:01:06.989
They wore thin rags for clothes and had no shoes.

14
00:01:08.289 --> 00:01:10.750
They saw the cut leather and got to work.

15
00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.091
And while they worked, they sang.

16
00:01:14.111 --> 00:01:19.772
We are helpful little elves.

17
00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:23.594
Helping others helps ourselves.

18
00:01:25.294 --> 00:01:29.555
The next morning a beautiful pair of shoes sat on the workbench.

19
00:01:30.895 --> 00:01:32.496
The shoemaker gasped.

20
00:01:33.804 --> 00:01:35.385
"Who made these shoes?"

21
00:01:35.405 --> 00:01:37.767
"What a miracle!"

22
00:01:38.188 --> 00:01:39.649
the shoemaker's wife said.

23
00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:43.372
That day a rich woman visited the shop.

24
00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:49.477
She loved the shoes and paid more than the shoemaker had expected.

25
00:01:51.579 --> 00:01:54.521
He was able to buy enough leather for two pairs of shoes.

26
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:59.606
That evening the shoemaker began cutting the leather.

27
00:01:59.626 --> 00:02:02.048
He yawned as he cut.

28
00:02:03.772 --> 00:02:08.273
"Dear, there's no need to work through the night," his wife said.

29
00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:11.494
The shoemaker nodded.

30
00:02:11.514 --> 00:02:15.275
"I'll just finish cutting the leather."

31
00:02:17.356 --> 00:02:21.297
When the shoemaker was finished, he left the leather on his workbench.

32
00:02:24.458 --> 00:02:26.458
He yawned again and went to bed.

33
00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:33.060
Once again the little elves visited the shop.

34
00:02:34.376 --> 00:02:36.618
They happily got to work, singing.

35
00:02:36.638 --> 00:02:41.662
We are helpful little elves.

36
00:02:41.962 --> 00:02:45.125
Helping others helps ourselves.

37
00:02:47.907 --> 00:02:52.891
The next morning two beautiful pairs of shoes sat finished on the workbench.

38
00:02:53.331 --> 00:02:56.794
"It happened again!"

39
00:02:57.235 --> 00:02:58.376
the shoemaker cried.

40
00:02:58.396 --> 00:03:03.480
"Someone must be trying to help us," his wife said.

41
00:03:05.236 --> 00:03:07.738
The two pairs of shoes quickly sold.

42
00:03:09.199 --> 00:03:12.461
Now there was enough money to buy leather for four pairs of shoes.

43
00:03:13.882 --> 00:03:16.544
For several more days, the pattern repeated.

44
00:03:18.085 --> 00:03:21.267
Eventually the shoemaker was no longer poor.

45
00:03:23.609 --> 00:03:28.132
One evening, not long before Christmas, the shoemaker was cutting leather.

46
00:03:28.152 --> 00:03:33.336
"Our fortunes have changed so quickly," his wife said.

47
00:03:34.636 --> 00:03:37.018
"I wonder who has been helping us."

48
00:03:37.038 --> 00:03:40.080
"Why don't we stay up tonight?"

49
00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:41.541
the shoemaker said.

50
00:03:41.561 --> 00:03:45.424
"We can see who our kind helpers are."

51
00:03:45.444 --> 00:03:48.486
"What a marvelous idea!"

52
00:03:48.967 --> 00:03:49.827
his wife said.

53
00:03:52.009 --> 00:03:52.809
They hid and waited.

54
00:03:54.651 --> 00:03:57.173
Before long the elves appeared on the workbench.

55
00:03:59.815 --> 00:04:04.354
As the elves sang and worked, the shoemaker and his wife whispered to each other.

56
00:04:04.374 --> 00:04:08.737
"Those poor creatures," she said.

57
00:04:08.757 --> 00:04:11.799
"Their clothes are worn out."

58
00:04:11.819 --> 00:04:16.443
"And they have no shoes," the shoemaker said.

59
00:04:16.463 --> 00:04:20.646
"They helped us, so we should help them.

60
00:04:20.666 --> 00:04:24.989
I have an idea!"

61
00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:29.272
On Christmas Eve the elves appeared again.

62
00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:33.882
When they climbed onto the workbench, they gasped.

63
00:04:35.143 --> 00:04:36.865
There was no leather cut for shoes.

64
00:04:38.366 --> 00:04:43.450
Instead there were two sets of fine clothes and two fine pairs of shoes.

65
00:04:44.571 --> 00:04:47.173
The elves quickly put everything on, singing.

66
00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:49.935
We helped them.

67
00:04:50.555 --> 00:04:52.017
We did, indeed.

68
00:04:52.777 --> 00:04:56.160
And they gave us the things we need.

69
00:04:58.076 --> 00:05:01.299
The shoemaker and his wife watched the elves shuffle away.

70
00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.541
The elves never visited the shop again.

71
00:05:06.463 --> 00:05:10.366
But the shoemaker and his wife never forgot their kind helpers.
